# Milestone: M3
# Covers: Mutex used as Tag via 'm:{ ... }' colon-scope notation; stop exception
#         during mutex critical section releases the mutex; nested detach inside mutex.
# deferred: v1.x — Mutex stdlib type not in v1.0 scope
# matrix-row: stdlib-mutex
#
# Reason:
#   The 'm:{ ... }' tag-scope notation on a Mutex requires Mutex to be usable as
#   a Tag (prototype inheritance chain — M4 object model) and the Lock/Mutex
#   acquire-on-entry / release-on-exit semantics (M6 stdlib).  Stop-exception
#   inside a critical section exercising the finally/cleanup path (mutex release
#   on stop) additionally depends on M5 scheduler integration.  'for&(var i: 4)'
#   parallel for (M5 chk driver).
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M6 with Mutex as Tag and M5 chk driver):
# # var m = Mutex.new() | {};
# # function f(name) { ... m: { sleep(1s) } } | {};
# # m.lock(); f("func1"), ... m.unlock(); ...
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/mutex/tagged.chk)
